(7676875, 1254916, 91360, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> Correct title, but the scene and feel is nothing like Salvador Dali''s painting.  In Dali''s the woman is peering out at the water and the viewer gets a sense of yearning for freedom or waiting on her mate to come home.  This woman''s pose is nothing like the depicted painting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>   https://www.wikiart.org/en/henri-matisse<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: Correct title, but the scene and feel is nothing like Salvador Dali''s painting.  In Dali''s the woman is peering out at the water and the viewer gets a sense of yearning for freedom or waiting on her mate to come home.  This woman''s pose is nothing like the depicted painting.      https://www.wikiart.org/en/henri-matisse', '2020-10-15 21:11:36.000000', NULL, 0),
